# Cloudflare applies these headers to every route.
# Content-Security-Policy beyond frame-ancestors is intentionally not set here — getting it
# right requires auditing every inline script (incl. Astro ClientRouter) and the Cloudflare
# Analytics beacon. Revisit a full CSP post-launch.
#
# frame-ancestors: who may iframe this site.
#   'self' is now the load-bearing one (2026-08-28). The Studio is EMBEDDED at
#   /studio on this same origin, so the Presentation tool's draft-preview iframe
#   (/preview/**) is a same-origin frame. Remove 'self' and live preview goes blank.
#   The https://*.sanity.studio / sanity.io entries are left in place only until the
#   old hosted mas-monograms.sanity.studio deploy is retired (docs/PENDING.md); the
#   localhost:3333/3334 entries served the old standalone `sanity dev` server, which
#   no longer exists — the Studio runs at localhost:4321/studio with `npm run dev`,
#   which is same-origin and therefore already covered by 'self'.
# Modern browsers prefer CSP frame-ancestors over X-Frame-Options when both are present.

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self' https://*.sanity.studio https://www.sanity.io https://*.sanity.io
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
